    "title": "RCB vs CSK: How has Virat Kohli fared against Chennai in the IPL?",
    "text": "As Royal Challengers Bengaluru gear up to face Chennai Super Kings in match 11 of IPL 2026, all eyes will once again be on Virat Kohli, who boasts a remarkable record against the five-time champions.The former RCB skipper has been one of the most consistent performers in IPL history and continues to dominate even in his 19th consecutive season with the franchise. Kohli began IPL 2026 on a strong note, scoring an unbeaten 69 off 38 balls against Sunrisers Hyderabad, underlining his enduring class.Virat Kohli’s Dominance Over CSKVirat Kohli holds the record for the most runs scored against Chennai Super Kings in IPL history. In 35 matches (34 innings), the RCB stalwart has amassed 1,146 runs at an impressive average of 38.2 against CSK.His highest score against Chennai is an unbeaten 90, and he has registered 10 fifty-plus scores against them, the most by any player against a single opponent in the tournament. Kohli is also on the verge of another milestone. He needs just 14 more runs to surpass his own record of 1,159 runs against Punjab Kings and become the player with the most runs against a single team in IPL history.Strong Record at ChinnaswamyAt the M. Chinnaswamy Stadium, Kohli has been particularly dominant against CSK. He has scored 389 runs at an average of 38.90, coupled with a striking strike rate of 149.04, significantly higher than his overall IPL strike rate.His ability to accelerate on a batting-friendly surface makes him a key threat for the CSK bowling attack once again. Kohli’s consistency against CSK has stood out over the years. In IPL 2025, he scored 93 runs in two innings against Chennai, playing a crucial role in RCB’s victories in both encounters during their title-winning campaign.Interestingly, Kohli has also made a minor contribution with the ball, picking up one wicket against CSK in IPL history.AdvertisementRCB vs CSK head-to-headMatches played: 36CSK wins: 22RCB wins: 13No result: 1In 36 meetings between the two sides, Chennai Super Kings have won 22 matches, while Royal Challengers Bengaluru have managed 13 victories, with one game ending in no result. 130037756Recent Form & MomentumWhile CSK leads the all-time record, the tide has shifted in favor of the defending champions Winning Streak: RCB has won their last 3 consecutive matches against CSK, including a clean sweep (2-0) during the 2025 season.Last 5 Meetings: RCB leads 3–2 in their most recent five encounters.Historic Win: In 2025, RCB ended a 17-year drought by defeating CSK at their home ground, the MA Chidambaram Stadium (Chepauk), by 50 runs.",
